    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμύ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>uninitiated, profane,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.51
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἀτέλεστος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					69c
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Ἀφροδίτης</span>
			<i>not admitted into mysteries</i> of Aphrodite, <i><span class="en">
				Aristaenet.
				1.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠδίνων,</span> of Artemis, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				36.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυήσεις ἀ.</span>
			<i>no true</i> initiations, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.156
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not closed, open,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Gym.</u>
				29
			</span></i> codd.; with play on both meanings, <i>leaky,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				493a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				493b
			</span></i>.</div>
